# Things I Want to Know More About

## Class 01 — Node Ecosystem

- How Node.js is used in larger real-world applications.
- How CI/CD changes when working on a development team.
- How automated testing fits into the development process.

## Class 02 — Express

- How middleware is used in production applications.
- How Express decides which middleware or route runs next.
- Better ways to organize routes, middleware, and error handlers as an application grows.

## Class 03 — Express REST API

- How REST APIs communicate with front-end applications.
- How to decide which HTTP status code should be returned.
- How to structure a larger API with multiple resources and routes.

## Class 04 — Data Modeling

- How to decide what information should become a model.
- When SQL is a better choice than NoSQL and vice versa.
- How Sequelize models relate to tables in PostgreSQL.
- How relationships between different models are created.

## Class 05 — Linked Lists

- When a Linked List is a better choice than an array.
- How `next` actually stores a reference to another Node in memory.
- How inserting and deleting Nodes changes the links between Nodes.
- How Linked Lists lead into more complex data structures such as stacks, queues, trees, and graphs.
- How Big O can be determined by looking at an algorithm.